note: Dodge! Move with the left and right arrow keys and dodge the falling balls.
note: Run it with: imagine examples/dodge.imagine      (or build it: imagine build examples/dodge.imagine)

use: window

a ball has:
  birth (a flat place)
  speed (a number)
and the universe said i love you

genesis:
  open a window with "Dodge!", 480, 640
  set player x to 240
  set balls to a list of balls
  set score to 0
  set best to 0
  try:
    load best from file "dodge best.json"
  if that went wrong:
    set best to 0
  set playing to yes
  while the window is open:
    if playing:
      if key held "left": set player x to player x minus 6
      if key held "right": set player x to player x plus 6
      set player x to clamp player x between 30 and 450
      if random number from 1 to 20 is 1: add a falling ball to balls
      set balls to every ball moved down from balls
      for each ball in balls:
        if hits the player with (ball, player x): set playing to no
      if not playing and score is more than best:
        set best to score
        save best to file "dodge best.json"
      set score to score plus 1
    otherwise if key held "space":
      set balls to a list of balls
      set score to 0
      set playing to yes
    consume the window with "#101828"
    for each ball in balls: draw a circle with existence of ball of horizontal, existence of ball of vertical, 14, "orange"
    draw a box with player x minus 30, 600, 60, 16, "#5ad1ff"
    draw words with "Score: " plus score, 12, 10, "white"
    draw words with "Best: " plus best, 380, 10, "white"
    if not playing: draw words with "Ouch! Press space to play again.", 120, 300, "yellow"
    show the frame
and the universe said i love you

to a falling ball, giving back a ball:
  set made to a new ball
  set birth of made to (random number from 20 to 460) horizontal -20 vertical
  set speed of made to random number from 3 to 8
  give back made
and the universe said i love you

to every ball moved down from, given balls (a list of balls), giving back a list of balls:
  set still falling to a list of balls
  for each ball in balls:
    set moved to ball
    set existence of moved to existence of ball plus 0 horizontal (speed of ball) vertical
    if existence of moved of vertical is less than 680: add moved to still falling
  give back still falling
and the universe said i love you

to hits the player, given ball (a ball) and player x (a number), giving back yes or no:
  set where to existence of ball
  give back where of vertical is more than 586 and where of vertical is less than 630 and where of horizontal is within 44 of player x
and the universe said i love you
